            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Carlos Concepci\u00f3n pleaded guilty to distributing five or more grams of crack cocaine and received a 19\u2011year sentence."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "0493778531f49b04b3d621e3ca0714e4d7430af55b1ad65b2ad8062b73fe200e",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-0493778531f4-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 43,
              "start": 43
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioner, Concepci\u00f3n sought a sentence reduction under Section\u202f404 of the First Step Act, which authorizes a limited reduction proceeding based on the Fair Sentencing Act\u2019s changes to crack\u2011cocaine sentencing."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "01c2a82ed903373e126e721864e3269469120233fee779908a05b86c3ab220b2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-01c2a82ed903-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The legal question was whether the First Step Act allows district courts to consider intervening changes of law or fact when exercising their discretion to reduce a sentence."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Background and Question",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
